{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0150"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge history/early-modern","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/history__early-modern.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",778],["+","queen herself went down in history with a sentence she never spoke. The story of a great princess who, told that the peasants had no bread, replied \"then let them eat brioche\" appears in the Confessions of Jean-Jacques Rousseau, written down in 1765 and published in 1782, when Maria Antonia was a nine-year-old girl in Vienna. Her enemies attached the line to her only later, and no evidence links it to her.\n\nThe "],["=",343]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",750],["+","Königin selbst ging mit einem Satz in die Geschichte ein, den sie nie gesagt hat. Die Geschichte von einer großen Prinzessin, die auf die Nachricht, die Bauern hätten kein Brot, antwortete, „dann sollen sie Brioche essen“, steht in den Bekenntnissen von Jean-Jacques Rousseau, niedergeschrieben 1765 und veröffentlicht 1782 – als Maria Antonia ein neunjähriges Mädchen in Wien war. Ihre Gegner hängten ihr den Satz erst später an, und kein Beleg verbindet ihn mit ihr.\n\nDie "],["=",329]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0150"},"reason":"a0150 body: \"most of them broke their word within weeks\" → \"several of them broke their word within months\" — Prussia invaded in Dec 1740, and the others joined in 1741 — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_the_Austrian_Succession","by":"enrich batch 091","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a0030-a1146.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_the_Austrian_Succession"}]},
